From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] local: drm/msm: serialize devcoredump reads

adreno_show_object() encodes a captured buffer to ascii85 on the first
read of a devcoredump, frees the raw copy and flags it encoded. The read
callback runs show() without any lock, so two processes reading the same
devcoredump at once both see the buffer unencoded, both encode it and both
free it:

  WARNING: mm/slub.c:6608 at free_large_kmalloc+0xb0/0xf8, CPU#2: cat/5264
   kvfree+0x44/0x60
   adreno_show_object+0x1f0/0x2a0 [msm]
   adreno_show+0x2b8/0x450 [msm]
   a6xx_show+0x6c/0x1380 [msm]
   msm_gpu_devcoredump_read+0x128/0x1e0 [msm]
  page dumped because: Not a kmalloc allocation

followed by a SLUB freelist BUG that killed both readers. It happened when
a udev-started saver and a second reader opened the same GPU page-fault
devcoredump in the same second.

Hold a mutex across the whole read. The debugfs gpu file captures its own
state, so it does not share buffers with a devcoredump.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -176,6 +176,13 @@
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEV_COREDUMP
+/*
+ * adreno_show_object() ascii85-encodes each captured buffer in place on the
+ * first read and frees the raw copy, so two readers of the same state must
+ * not run show() at the same time.
+ */
+static DEFINE_MUTEX(msm_gpu_devcoredump_read_lock);
+
 static ssize_t msm_gpu_devcoredump_read(char *buffer, loff_t offset,
 		size_t count, void *data, size_t datalen)
 {
@@ -184,6 +191,8 @@
 	struct drm_printer p;
 	struct msm_gpu_state *state;
 
+	guard(mutex)(&msm_gpu_devcoredump_read_lock);
+
 	state = msm_gpu_crashstate_get(gpu);
 	if (!state)
 		return 0;
